<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<div class="note"><b class="h">Local claim risks in Fresno</b><ul class="chips"><li>Extreme heat</li><li>Wind</li><li>Wildfire smoke</li><li>Water leaks</li><li>Agricultural buildings</li></ul><p class="hoods"><b>Neighborhoods we often work in:</b> Tower District, Fig Garden, Woodward Park, Sunnyside, Old Fig, Bullard</p></div>

<h2>Heat, wind and roofs</h2>
<p>Summer temperatures in Fresno regularly exceed 100°F, which accelerates shingle aging, dries out seals and stresses HVAC equipment. When a storm or wind event damages a roof, carriers sometimes attribute the damage to age. An insurance appraiser in Fresno has to document storm damage carefully enough to separate it from wear.</p>
<h2>Wildfire and smoke from the Sierra</h2>
<p>The 2020 Creek Fire burned across the Sierra in Fresno and Madera counties, destroying hundreds of structures in mountain communities and blanketing the valley in smoke for weeks. Foothill and mountain homes face direct fire risk, while valley homes can have smoke infiltration claims during major fire seasons.</p>
<h2>Neighborhoods and housing</h2>
<p>The Tower District has 1920s and 1930s homes with stucco and Spanish details. Fig Garden and Old Fig have larger homes on big lots under mature trees. Woodward Park and the northeast have newer subdivisions with tile roofs. Clovis, next door, adds a large stock of newer homes. Many properties also include pools, outbuildings and solar systems that need separate attention in a claim.</p>
<h2>Agricultural and commercial property</h2>
<p>Fresno County is one of the most productive farming counties in the country. Packing sheds, barns, cold storage and equipment buildings are often insured on farm or commercial policies with different valuation terms. We value these structures with attention to their specialized systems.</p>
<h3>Water losses</h3>
<p>Slab leaks and failed supply lines are common across Fresno’s housing stock, and evaporative coolers and HVAC condensate lines add their own leak risks.</p>

<h2>Services available in Fresno</h2>
<p>Every California Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in Fresno and the rest of Fresno County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/policyholder-appraiser-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/home-claim-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/commercial-hoa-claim-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/roof-damage-appraisal/">Roof Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/santa-ana-wind-damage-appraisal/">Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/atmospheric-river-storm-claim-appraisal/">Atmospheric River &amp; Storm Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/water-leak-claim-appraisal/">Water Leak Claim Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Fresno property owners</h2><div class="qa"><details><summary>The carrier says my roof damage is just age. What can I do?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Document fresh damage with dated photos and a professional inspection. If coverage is accepted for part of the damage, appraisal can resolve the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you handle farm buildings?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Yes. We value barns, packing sheds and other agricultural structures, often insured under farm or commercial policies.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you serve Clovis and Madera?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Yes, along with Visalia, Hanford, Madera and the foothill communities.</p></div></details></div>
